  "lineage": "Industrialised from 1934 onward by George Owen Squier's Muzak Corporation in New York and later Seattle, elevator music is purpose-recorded instrumental background scoring — light string orchestra, muted brass, celeste, vibraphone and organ playing popular standards at deliberately even dynamics, no vocals, no drum accents, arranged in fifteen-minute 'stimulus progression' blocks of graded tempo and distributed by leased telephone line and tape cartridge to lobbies, factories and lifts.",
